# Independent Claim

**Claim 1.** An image sensor comprising:

a semiconductor substrate having a first surface and a second surface opposite to the first surface;

a photodiode disposed in the semiconductor substrate, the photodiode configured to generate photocharges in response to incident light received through the first surface;

a floating diffusion region disposed in the semiconductor substrate and spaced apart from the photodiode;

a charge storage region disposed in the semiconductor substrate between the photodiode and the floating diffusion region, the charge storage region configured to temporarily store the photocharges transferred from the photodiode;

a first transfer gate disposed on the second surface of the semiconductor substrate between the photodiode and the charge storage region, the first transfer gate configured to control transfer of the photocharges from the photodiode to the charge storage region;

a second transfer gate disposed on the second surface of the semiconductor substrate between the charge storage region and the floating diffusion region, the second transfer gate configured to control transfer of the photocharges from the charge storage region to the floating diffusion region, the second transfer gate being spaced apart from the first transfer gate; and

a light-shielding member disposed over the first transfer gate and the second transfer gate,

wherein the light-shielding member includes a horizontal portion extending along the second surface of the semiconductor substrate and a protruding portion extending from the horizontal portion into a space between the first transfer gate and the second transfer gate toward the semiconductor substrate, the protruding portion configured to block incident light from reaching the charge storage region through the space between the first transfer gate and the second transfer gate.
